{# Sub-Query Decomposition: Split complex query for parallel retrieval #}
You are an expert AI assistant. Answer the following query by splitting it into sub-queries.

<query>
{{ user_input|default(query|default("")) }}
</query>

{% set decomposition_method = decomposition_method|default("semantic") %}
{% set num_subqueries = num_subqueries|default(3) %}
{% set iteration = iteration|default(1) %}
{% set max_iterations = max_iterations|default(5) %}

<decomposition_strategy>
Decomposition strategy: {{ decomposition_method }}
</decomposition_strategy>

{% if iteration == 1 %}
<phase>
Step 1: Decompose into sub-queries
</phase>

Break this complex query into {{ num_subqueries }} smaller, distinct sub-questions.

Each sub-query should be:
- Clear and self-contained
- Answerable with a single retrieval pass
- Without overlapping information needs
- In logical order if dependencies exist

<sub_queries>
List your {{ num_subqueries }} sub-queries
</sub_queries>
{% elif iteration <= num_subqueries + 1 %}
<phase>
Step {{ iteration - 1 }}: Answer sub-query {{ iteration - 1 }}
</phase>

<sub_query_answer>
Your answer to sub-query {{ iteration - 1 }}
</sub_query_answer>
{% else %}
<phase>
Final step: Synthesis
</phase>

<final_synthesis>
Synthesize all sub-question answers into a comprehensive final answer to the original query.
</final_synthesis>
{% endif %}
